    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the clear offensive anchor with a score of 83.29. He faces a favorable matchup against a pitcher with a 4.41 xERA, bolstered by a 14% platoon edge and a prime #3 slot in the order that maximizes his RBI and run-scoring potential. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** (72.67) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.41) represent elite daily options; **Drake Baldwin** benefits significantly from leading off and a high xwOBA (0.386), while **Jackson Merrill** enjoys a robust 13% platoon advantage against a pitcher with a 4.58 xERA, positioning him as a high-upside play for our 5x5 needs. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also warrants attention at 69.74; despite a tougher matchup against a 3.58 xERA southpaw, his intrinsic power and placement in the #2 spot make him an essential start.\n\nThe decision to bench **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (48.16) was the most difficult, as he narrowly missed the cut behind **Nasim Nunez**. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers utility, his heavy penalty for a same-side platoon disadvantage and a bottom-order lineup spot outweighed his base projections. We remain wary of several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Denzer Guzman**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Wade Meckler**. While they benefit from wind-aided conditions, their scores remain precarious; **Wade Meckler** in particular faces a 9% penalty due to a platoon disadvantage against the starting lefty, and he should be monitored closely if final lineups show a drop in batting order. Finally, while **Andy Pages** and **Heliot Ramos** are viable, their output may be slightly suppressed by elite defensive catchers today, underscoring the need to capitalize on the high-probability spots occupied by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**.",
